The sequence provided up to the 14th term is:

**1, 1, 3, 12, 55, 273, 1428, 7752, 43263, 246675, 1430715, 8414640, 49586220, 297523320, 1822766520**

This sequence is known in the OEIS (Online Encyclopedia of Integer Sequences) as **A002467**, which counts the **number of permutations of [n] with no increasing subsequence of length 3** (i.e., permutations avoiding the pattern 123). 

The recurrence relation for this sequence is:

$$
a(n) = (n + 1) \cdot a(n - 1) - \binom{n - 1}{2} \cdot a(n - 2)
$$

Using this recurrence, the next term (the 15th term in the sequence, for $ n = 14 $) is computed as:

$$
a(15) = 15 \cdot a(14) - \binom{13}{2} \cdot a(13)
$$

$$
a(15) = 15 \cdot 1822766520 - \frac{13 \cdot 12}{2} \cdot 297523320
$$

$$
a(15) = 27341497800 - 78 \cdot 297523320
$$

$$
a(15) = 27341497800 - 23206818960
$$

$$
a(15) = 4134678840
$$

